## Issues / observations (none blocking)
1. **Too easy / flat difficulty (design, minor).** Only one obstacle at a time, edge gap >= 0.9 s, speed caps at ~28 s (330 -> 560), one obstacle shape. Every timing from 0.08 s to 0.4 s before contact survived, so there is almost no way to die once awake; the run is long and repetitive. Suggest a tighter cap on the gap at high speed or occasional paired obstacles if "fun" is a priority; the producer decides.
2. **High score does not update live (minor).** During a run score 500 sat next to 最高分 20 (05-capped-speed-midplay.png); best only updates on death. Players beating their record get no feedback until they die.
3. **Instant restart on Space after death (minor, from code reading, not exercised by a human).** `jump()` restarts the moment state is `over`, with no delay, so a player who is still tapping when they hit an obstacle may skip the game-over screen unseen. A ~0.3-0.5 s lockout would avoid this.
4. Obstacles are pure rectangles, player a plain square, no jump/death feedback or sound; acceptable for the brief (art in code).
5. Not tested: touch input, tabs/focus loss, very small windows, browsers other than headless Chromium, Safari/Firefox localStorage behaviour under file://.

## Verdict
Playable, completable loop; all five brief requirements observed working except the zip-structure part of requirement 5, which I could not inspect. No blocker found in the game itself.
